Package: paralogswap
Title: Title: Detect Paralog Substitution Events in Cross-Species Single-Cell RNA-Seq Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Clara", "Tucker", , "ClaraC.Tucker@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects paralog substitution events in cross-species single-cell
    RNA-seq data without requiring cell-type annotation. Cross-species
    correspondence is derived from expression rather than supplied as labels:
    each species is clustered independently, clusters are matched across
    species over a one-to-one ortholog bridge, and metacells are matched within
    matched clusters. Each gene is then correlated against its ortholog and its
    paralogs over that grid, flagging genes whose paralog tracks the
    cross-species pattern better than the annotated ortholog. Homology is read
    from curated Ensembl Compara orthology via 'biomaRt', retaining the full
    graph including one-to-many and many-to-many edges, with support for
    user-supplied corrections where curated calls are incomplete or erroneous.
